{"mentions":[{"name":"WordPress","rank":1,"sentiment":"positive","in_entity_list":false,"rationale":"Best default for editorial and B2B teams because it readily supports crawlable content publishing and automated freshness workflows."},{"name":"Shopify","rank":2,"sentiment":"positive","in_entity_list":false,"rationale":"Best fit for commerce because product pages, sitemaps, and baseline product structured data are supplied by the platform."},{"name":"Drupal","rank":3,"sentiment":"positive","in_entity_list":false,"rationale":"Best fit for large, multilingual, highly governed content estates that need explicit content modeling and technical control."},{"name":"Contentful","rank":4,"sentiment":"positive","in_entity_list":false,"rationale":"A strong composable option when paired with a technically sound server-rendered or static front end."},{"name":"Webflow","rank":5,"sentiment":"positive","in_entity_list":false,"rationale":"A practical option for smaller marketing sites because it provides sitemap, robots, and schema controls without extensive engineering."},{"name":"server-side rendering or static-site generation","rank":6,"sentiment":"positive","in_entity_list":false,"rationale":"This delivery approach makes the primary page content immediately available as HTML rather than relying on crawler JavaScript execution."},{"name":"client-only single-page applications","rank":7,"sentiment":"negative","in_entity_list":false,"rationale":"This approach adds crawl and rendering risk when important content is not present in the initial HTML."},{"name":"semantic HTML","rank":8,"sentiment":"positive","in_entity_list":false,"rationale":"Semantic headings, lists, tables, and links make page meaning and answer extraction clearer for both people and machines."},{"name":"XML sitemaps","rank":9,"sentiment":"positive","in_entity_list":false,"rationale":"They improve discovery of canonical, indexable URLs and support faster auditing of a site’s crawl surface."},{"name":"robots.txt","rank":10,"sentiment":"neutral","in_entity_list":false,"rationale":"It is essential for permitting intended crawlers but can accidentally prevent discovery when misconfigured."},{"name":"IndexNow","rank":11,"sentiment":"positive","in_entity_list":false,"rationale":"It is useful for notifying participating engines when URLs are added, changed, or removed, particularly for freshness."}],"sources":["https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/ai-optimization-guide","https://developers.google.com/search/docs/essentials/technical?hl=en","https://help.openai.com/en/articles/12627856-publishers-and-developers-faq","https://www.bing.com/webmasters/help/url-submission-62f2860b","https://blogs.bing.com/webmaster/February-2026/Introducing-AI-Performance-in-Bing-Webmaster-Tools-Public-Preview","https://wordpress.org/plugins/indexnow/","https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/seo/find-site-map?inf_contact_key=3d392e83ba9b80d97dcf39e68f356c0f","https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/markets/seo","https://www.drupal.org/project/simple_sitemap","https://www.drupal.org/docs/contributed-modules/schemaorg-metatag","https://help.webflow.com/hc/en-us/articles/33961355371667-Create-a-sitemap-in-Webflow","https://help.webflow.com/hc/en-us/articles/45766917223955-Add-schema-markup-in-Webflow-to-improve-SEO-and-AEO","https://www.contentful.com/seo-guide/technical-seo/"],"answer_summary":"**Short answer:** platform choice helps, but no CMS is inherently “AI-readable.” As of August 18, 2026, choose **WordPress** for most editorial/B2B sites, **Shopify** for commerce, **Drupal** for large multilingual or governed estates, **Contentful** only when your team can pair it with server-side rendering or static-site generation, and **Webflow** for smaller marketing sites; each can expose crawlable pages, but WordPress and Drupal give the broadest operational control, Shopify has the strongest commerce defaults, and Webflow is the easiest marketer-led option. Shopify automatically produces sitemaps and includes product microdata in supported themes; Webflow can generate and publish a sitemap through robots.txt and now offers schema controls; Drupal’s ecosystem supports JSON-LD, multilingual sitemaps, and IndexNow; and WordPress has a Microsoft-maintained IndexNow plugin for automatic URL-change notification. ([help.shopify.com](https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/seo/find-site-map?inf_contact_key=3d392e83ba9b80d97dcf39e68f356c0f&utm_source=openai))

**What actually makes the site legible to answer engines:** require public, canonical pages that return HTTP 200; put the complete primary answer, product facts, author/date, and supporting evidence in the initial HTML; use clear semantic HTML and stable headings; publish XML sitemaps; manage canonical, noindex, and robots directives centrally; emit accurate schema for supported search features; avoid cookie walls, login gates, WAF/CDN bot challenges, and content that appears only after client-side JavaScript; allow **OAI-SearchBot** if you want content eligible for ChatGPT summaries; and implement **IndexNow** where your platform or deployment stack supports it. Google explicitly says its AI features use the same crawl/index foundation as Search and require crawlable, indexed, snippet-eligible pages—not a special “AI schema”; it also cautions that JavaScript SEO is more complex. OpenAI says public sites can appear in ChatGPT Search and that publishers should not block OAI-SearchBot for content to be included in summaries/snippets, while Bing recommends IndexNow for automated, faster change notification. ([developers.google.com](https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/ai-optimization-guide?utm_source=openai))

**Buying recommendation:** do not replatform solely for AI visibility. Score your current platform against five non-negotiables—server-rendered primary content, editable robots/meta/canonicals, complete sitemap control, structured fields for entities/products/authors/dates, and a publish-time webhook path to refresh discovery—and migrate only if it cannot meet them; a well-configured WordPress, Shopify, Drupal, Contentful, or Webflow site will outperform a poorly implemented site on a supposedly more “AI-native” platform."}

